# ── REPO HYGIENE. Enforced by the `hygiene` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
# ⚠ THESE RULES USED TO LIVE ONLY IN .git/info/exclude, WHICH IS LOCAL AND NEVER COMMITTED — so a
# fresh clone, a second machine and CI itself were all unprotected. Measured 2026-08-06 across
# gated, gated-uat and mori: all three, same gap, all three public.
# ⚠ AND THIS FILE IS THE GUARD, NOT THE ENFORCEMENT. .gitignore stops an ACCIDENT; it does not
# detect an artefact that is ALREADY tracked, and `git add -f` walks straight past it. The CI job
# therefore asserts on `git ls-files` — on what IS tracked — and checks this file separately.
.gitnexus/
.venv/
node_modules/
.env
.secrets
